\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The second moments of residual log earnings by family background. Variance in each wave (panel a) and autocovariance by lag, averaged over waves (panel b), for advantaged and less advantaged children, with 95 percent bootstrap intervals (200 replications, clustered on person). The 2,523 children with at least three waves; residuals are demeaned within group and year (wave sizes 1,319, 1,049, 2,197, 2,083, and 2,001). Averages over waves weight each wave pair by the inverse of its bootstrap variance. Intervals overlap at every lag; the longest lags decide the permanent--transitory split of Table~\ref {tab:md}.}}{13}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
